# Ground Truth and Baselines

- Every task has a trusted reference under `solution/` that derives its answer
  from disclosed inputs and produces the same artifact shape as agents.
- Deterministic-rubric oracle target is `1.0`; continuous reference target is
  `0.5 ± 0.05`. Never lower the oracle target to make a task difficult.
- Trusted CI/ground-truth runs inference only; continuous tasks commit an
  inference entrypoint plus digest-bound strategy/model artifacts.
- Add naive/no-op and, where required, degenerate baselines that are ready to
  measure without training.
- MuJoCo requires H.264 `rendering.mp4` at `1280x720`; any task may declare
  reviewer media through `[ground_truth].render_outputs`.
- Local `--runtime ground-truth` is development preflight. Trusted CI generates
  authoritative proof/lock evidence from the immutable PR. Do not commit local
  generated proof/lock files; commit declared reviewed media when required.
- Regenerate the oracle, baselines, plan/calibration, and trusted evidence after
  any grading-input change.

Read `ground-truth-oracle` and `docs/GROUND_TRUTH.md`.
